### Overview

Let’s pin this into a **concrete, implementation-ready storage model** using **PostgreSQL + JSONB**, aligned tightly with your 10D engine.

> “This core logic manages the ten-vector state (x, y, z, w, v, u, q, p, s, f) and enables total system variance analysis.”  
> “Dimensions not in selected_axes are treated as PROC-046 metadata.”

---

### 1. Core table: 10D nodes

Each row = one 10D entity, with strict indexing baked in.

```sql
CREATE TABLE ten_d_nodes (
    id              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    label           TEXT NOT NULL,

    -- Strict 10D scalar fields
    x               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    y               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    z               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    w               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    v               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    u               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    q               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    p               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    s               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
    f               DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,

    -- Derived metrics
    total_system_variance  DOUBLE PRECISION,
    last_delta_axis        TEXT,
    last_delta_value       DOUBLE PRECISION,

    -- Full 10D vector cache (for LLM / tooling)
    state_vector    DOUBLE PRECISION[] CHECK (cardinality(state_vector) = 10)
);
```

**Notes:**

- `state_vector[1..10]` is **locked** to `[x,y,z,w,v,u,q,p,s,f]` (enforces “Never reorder the vector.”).  
- `total_system_variance` corresponds to the 10D Euclidean distance metric.

