### 2. Entanglement graph storage

> “This engine forces changes in target dimensions based on a source dimension’s delta.”

```sql
CREATE TYPE bond_type AS ENUM ('linear', 'inverse');

CREATE TABLE entanglement_bonds (
    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    node_id         TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ten_d_nodes(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    source_dim      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (source_dim IN ('x','y','z','w','v','u','q','p','s','f')),
    target_dim      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (target_dim IN ('x','y','z','w','v','u','q','p','s','f')),
    ratio           DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL DEFAULT 1.0,
    type            bond_type NOT NULL DEFAULT 'linear',

    proc_ref        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PROC-048'
);

-- Optional: prevent self-bonds and duplicates
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX entanglement_unique
ON entanglement_bonds (node_id, source_dim, target_dim);
```

**Recursion limit (PROC‑049)** is enforced in logic, but you can track it:

```sql
CREATE TABLE entanglement_settings (
    node_id         TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES ten_d_nodes(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    max_recursion   INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1  -- PROC-049
);
```

